  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Kenya: Judiciary Support Programme (JSP)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Direct beneficiaries: Judiciary (Family Division of the High Court, Kadhis Courts                and Magistrates Courts), Judiciary departments (Directorate of Public Affairs and Communication,                Directorate of Planning and Organizational Performance, Chief Registrar of the Judiciary, Small Claims                Courts, Court Annexed Mediation Secretariat, Mediation Accreditation Committee, Rules Committee and                Kenya Judiciary Academy), National Council on Administration of Justice (Special Taskforce on Children                Matters). Indirect beneficiaries: Justice seekers.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aimed to enhance access to justice through increased responsiveness of                the Judiciary to the needs of justice seekers in Kenya.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To enhance the capacity of the Judiciary: 1) to deliver fair, effective and                representative justice outcomes; 2) to respond to the specific justice needs of women, youth and                children; and 3) to monitor and communicate results and pathways to justice.</narrative>
  </description>
